51689f8dd1d3e1472456b658f620dcb2  var/dev_fbctrl_HEAD.c
fix.c CMP SEC: CLEAN
T_D2_mask63      D2: bit 63 masked before the compare
T_D3_pwron       D3: a refusal stores the value when the previous selector is 0 (power-on)
T_D3_ctor1       D3 extra (grok): the constructor selects port 1 at power-on
T_D4b_cmdrearm   D4: the latch cleared on entry to fbctrl_command()
T_D6_rdbit32     D6: the PORT read ORs bit 32
T_D7a_sub4zero   D7: selector 0 refused for sb/sh (len < 4)
T_D7b_sdzero     D7: selector 0 refused for sd (len == 8)
T_D7c_shzero     D7 extra: selector 0 refused for sh only (len == 2)
T_D8_or1         D8: the refusal ORs 1 into the previous selector
T_D9a_only9      D9: announce only for the value 9
T_D9b_mod10      D9: the latch counts modulo 10 (re-announces on the 11th refusal)
T_D9c_serial1    D9: announce only on the machine with serial_nr 1
T_D10_print0     D10: the diagnostic prints 0, not the refused value
T_D11a_y1one     D11: GET_RESOLUTION (no X11) sets Y1 to 1
T_D11b_y1keep    D11 extra: GET_RESOLUTION (no X11) leaves Y1 untouched
T_X_ann6         extra (Astra A-silence): an ACCEPTED selector 6 announces (once)
T_X_w8           extra (grok F2 #7): the boundary 8 refused only for 4-byte writes
M_revert         FLOOR-b: HEAD's PORT arm verbatim (store, then warn)
M_gt             d: >= becomes >
M_u32            d: compare on (uint32_t)idata
M_i32            d: compare on (int)idata
M_i64            d: compare on (int64_t)idata
M_decl           d: idata declared int64_t
M_mod33          d: compare on idata % 2^33
M_bit            d: a bit test for the bound
M_wide           d: refusal only for writes of 4+ bytes
M_acc4           d: accept only 4-byte writes
M_rej2           d: legal selector 2 never accepted
M_and5           d: the refusal rewrites the previous selector (&= 5)
M_reset0         d: the refusal resets the selector to 0
M_clamp          d: the refusal stores idata & 7
M_store          d: the refusal stores the value anyway
M_latch0         d: the latch never set (announce every time)
M_latchinv       d: the latch test inverted (never announce)
M_latchcnt       d: the latch counts (announces on the 3rd, 5th, ...)
M_perval         d: a per-value latch (announce when the value changes)
M_debug          d: the announce demoted to debug()
M_ann_any        d: the announce fires on ACCEPTED writes too
M_reflatch       d: the refusal only until the first announce (later ones stored)
M_acclatch       d: accepts only until the first refusal
M_static         e (disclosed): a process-global latch
M_noguard        e (disclosed): the DATA arm's range check deleted
